# KAPLAY Optimization Reference

## Core principles

- Choose collision strategy appropriate to world shape and movement patterns.
- Avoid unnecessary game object creation for purely visual/static rendering.
- Remove or hide off-screen entities to reduce update/draw cost.

## Practical tactics

- Use `offscreen({ destroy: true })` for throwaway entities (projectiles/effects).
- Use `offscreen({ hide: true, pause: true })` for large sparse maps.
- Prefer local object timers and local input handlers where lifecycle-scoped behavior is desired.

## Maintainability/perf balance

- Global timers/handlers can leak behavior after object destruction.
- Object-local APIs are safer for state machines and scene-local logic.
- Keep asset sizes and draw count in check before adding new effects.
